To add collection of RF monitoring data from buses and other endpoints.

Mothership boss:

0. Pick a bus, changing XXXX to the appropriate value:

   tarball=/usr/testbed/tmp/syncthing/bus-XXXX.tar.gz
   aggregate=bus-XXXX

1. Copy over the appropriate tarball (TBD):

   sudo scp $tarball boss.$aggregate.powderwireless.net:/tmp/st.tar.gz

2. Create the mirror directory where aggregate data goes, along with the
   marker:

   sudo mkdir -p /usr/testbed/www/rfmonitor-mobile/$aggregate/.stfolder
   sudo chown -R elabman:tbadmin /usr/testbed/www/rfmonitor-mobile/$aggregate



Aggregate boss:

1. Enable the "global" syncthing daemon, append this to the aggregate boss
   node's /etc/rc.conf:

   sudo ed /etc/rc.conf
   $a

# Syncthing for Powder RF data collection
syncthing_enable="YES"
syncthing_home="/usr/testbed/etc/syncthing"
syncthing_log_file="/usr/testbed/log/syncthing.log"
syncthing_user="elabman"
syncthing_group="tbadmin"
.
   w
   q

2. Install the syncthing config for the aggregate boss.

   sudo mkdir -m 700 /usr/testbed/etc/syncthing
   sudo tar -C /usr/testbed/etc/syncthing -xzf /tmp/st.tar.gz
   sudo chown -R elabman:tbadmin /usr/testbed/etc/syncthing
   sudo rm /tmp/st.tar.gz

3. Mark the data directory so that syncthing knows we really intended it
   to operate on the directory:

   sudo mkdir /usr/testbed/www/rfmonitor/.stfolder
   sudo chown elabman:tbadmin /usr/testbed/www/rfmonitor/.stfolder

   Nothing goes into this directory, syncthing just makes sure it exists.
   If you start up syncthing and it doesn't appear to be doing anything
   (no files show up in the mirror directory on mothership boss), then
   it is probably because this subdir is missing.

4. Start em up and see if there was anything obviously wrong:

   sudo /usr/local/etc/rc.d/syncthing start
   sleep 1
   tail -50 /usr/testbed/log/syncthing.log

To monitor what is going on:

Syncthing has a GUI that listens just on localhost, but you can do a port
forward on your local machine if you want to look at it:

   ssh -N -L 9090:127.0.0.1:8384 boss.$aggregate.powderwireless.net &

and then go to "localhost:9090" in your browser.

You can do the same with the boss.emulab.net syncthing as well, running
a port forward on boss.emulab.net.
